===Pronunciation===
* {{a|UK}} {{IPA|en|/ˈtɛm.pə.ɹə.mənt/|/ˈtɛm.pɹə.mənt/|/ˈtɛm.pə.mənt/}}
* {{a|US}} {{IPA|en|/ˈtɛm.pɚ.ə.mənt/|/ˈtɛm.pɹə.mənt/|/ˈtɛm.pɚ.mənt/}}<ref>{{R:Dictionary.com}}</ref><ref>{{R:MWO}}</ref>
* {{audio|en|LL-Q1860 (eng)-Vealhurl-temperament.wav|Audio (Southern England)}}

===Noun===
{{en-noun|~}}

# A person's usual [[manner]] of [[thinking]], [[behaving]] or [[reacting]].
#* {{quote-book
|en
|year=1928
|author=w:Franklin D. Roosevelt
|title=The Happy Warrior Alfred E. Smith
|url=https://archive.org/details/happywarrioralfr006717mbp/
|publisher=w:Houghton Mifflin
|OCLC=769015
|OL=6719278M
|page=13
|pageurl=https://archive.org/details/happywarrioralfr006717mbp/page/n23/
|text=President Taft did not have the '''temperament''' either to dominate or to work with his Congress.}}
# A [[tendency]] to become [[irritable]] or [[angry]].
# {{lb|en|music}} The [[altering]] of certain [[interval]]s from their [[correct]] [[value]]s in order to [[improve]] the moving from [[key]] to key.
# {{lb|en|psychology}}  Individual differences in behavior that are biologically based and are relatively independent of learning, system of values and attitudes.
# {{lb|en|obsolete}} A [[moderate]] and [[proportionable]] [[mixture]] of elements or ingredients in a [[compound]]; the condition in which elements are mixed in their proper proportions.
#* '''1624''', {{w|John Donne}}, ''{{w|Devotions Upon Emergent Occasions}}'', Meditation XVIII., in ''The Complete Poetry and Selected Prose of John Donne'', ed. Charles M. Coffin, New York: Modern Library (1952), pp. 442-444:
#*: If I will aske meere Philosophers, what the soule is, I shall finde amongst them, that will tell me, it is nothing, but the '''temperament''' and harmony, and just and equall composition of the Elements in the body, which produces all those faculties which we ascribe to the soule […]
# {{lb|en|obsolete}} Any state or condition as determined by the proportion of its ingredients or the manner in which they are mixed; [[consistence]], [[composition]]; [[mixture]].

